      {
        "id": "notes",
        "position": [
          2,
          1
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**SP05 \u2014 Add shifted impulse responses**  \n**Does filtering a sum equal adding the shifted responses?** Run **2 s at 20 Hz**.  \nKernel h=[1, 0.5, \u22120.25]. At n=4\u20268 predict 1, 0.5, \u22120.75, \u22120.25, 0.125 V; difference stays zero.  \nChange weight factor \u22120.5 \u2192 0.75; predict the overlap at n=6. All six Delay states start at zero. Zoom to read the three rows.  \n[Open SP05 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP05-convolution/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT teaching materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_lec08/) \u00b7 [S7 timing and integrators](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/INTEGRATORS.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1789,
          "height": 300,
          "font_size": 20
        }
      }
    ]
